meta {
  name: List placements in this syllabus
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/placements?curriculum_id={{curriculumId}}&status=proposed
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.count: eq 2
  res.body.page.has_more: eq false
}

docs {
  The review queue: everything mapped to this syllabus that nobody has agreed
  with yet. Filter by origin=inferred as well and it is the machine's
  suggestions only, which is the list a teacher is actually asked to work
  through.

  Reading a placement needs both grants. The row names a content item, so a
  caller with placement access but no library access could learn which books
  exist by reading the mappings; this list is narrowed by what the caller may
  read in the library as well as by what they may read here.
}
